# Local QA screenshots (not for repo).
#
# KHANDAQ (re-audit 2026-08-22, W-02): anchored to the repository root. A bare `assets/` matches
# EVERY directory of that name at any depth, so it silently swallowed web/assets — the site's own
# icons and, once the fonts were self-hosted, 873 KiB of woff2 the pages now depend on. The seven
# icons already in the repository were force-added past this rule, which is why nobody noticed. A
# clean checkout would have deployed a site with no webfonts at all, and the CSP that forbids the
# Google fallback would have made that permanent rather than merely slow.
/assets/

# Logs and local ops
*.log
docs/network-deploy-logs/
docs/smoke-test-screenshots/

# Internal / non-public documentation (English public docs are whitelisted below)
docs/**
!docs/BUILDING.md
!docs/NETWORK.md
!docs/BOOTSTRAP.md
!docs/PUSH_RELAY.md
!docs/SECURITY_AUDIT_RETEST.md
# KHANDAQ (re-audit 2026-08-22): both are public by design — the permission matrix is what the
# manifest gate compares against, and the signing runbook is what a user follows to verify a
# download. Without these lines `git add -A` silently skips them and the gate fails in CI, which is
# how this was found rather than by anyone noticing the files were missing.
!docs/ANDROID-PERMISSIONS.md
!docs/DESKTOP-SIGNING.md
# KHANDAQ (re-review 2026-08-22, KQ-01/KQ-02): the compatibility matrix is what publishes the legacy
# retirement date, and the evidence file is the measured relay state a release actually shipped
# against. Both are the answer to a finding, so both have to leave this machine.
!docs/PUSH-COMPATIBILITY.md
!docs/release-evidence/
!docs/release-evidence/*.json

# Отчёты аудитов и разбор находок: ради них всё и делалось, они обязаны быть в репозитории.
!docs/audits/
!docs/audits/*.md

# Разрешения, которые библиотеки добавляют при слиянии манифеста: по этому списку
# check-policy-claims.py сверяет политику конфиденциальности там, где сборки нет (CI).
!docs/android-merge-injected-permissions.txt

